description: Persist user remarks into .cursor/rules without waiting to be asked
alwaysApply: true
---

# Capture user remarks as rules

When the user states a standing preference, a correction, or a “don’t
do X / do Y instead” remark, **write or update a `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`
immediately**. Do not wait for “add that to the rules” / “note that”.

Treat it as a rule if it should apply on later turns (casts, wrappers,
host vs library, typing, decomposition, …). One concern per file;
update an existing rule when the remark belongs there.

Do **not** persist one-off task instructions (“rename this function”,
“commit these files”).
